# Redoubt doh-mullvad-migration.patch  (Android)
#
# Upstream files touched
# -----------------------
#   mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/Core.kt  (1 call, top of Core.engine)
#   mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/HomeActivity.kt     (1 call in onResume)
#   mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/settings/doh/DohSettingsProvider.kt
#   mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/settings/doh/DefaultDohSettingsProviderTest.kt
#     (both: privacy-defaults.patch's provider catalog, minus Mullvad)
# New files
#   mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/lw/DohProviderMigration.kt
#   mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values/lw_doh_migration.xml
#   mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/lw/DohProviderMigrationTest.kt
#
# Line numbers are from the ESR tree (firefox-153.4.0esr, ./version.android),
# AFTER the patches listed before this one in assets/patches/android.txt.
#
#
# What it is
# -----------
# Mullvad is discontinuing its DNS over HTTPS service. The 153 ESR beta offered
# "Mullvad (No Filtering)" (https://dns.mullvad.net/dns-query) in the Fenix DoH
# picker -- privacy-defaults.patch's hand-kept copy of doh-rollout.provider-list
# -- and Fenix persists the choice in fenix_preferences
# (pref_key_doh_provider_uri, beside the mode in pref_key_doh_settings_mode).
# When the service stops, such a profile loses DoH in Increased Protection and
# loses name resolution altogether in Max Protection (TRR_MODE_ONLY).
#
# Three changes:
#   1. Core.engine, before DefaultSettings reads settings.dohProviderUrl, calls
#      DohProviderMigration.migrate. Once per profile, a stored provider whose
#      host is dns.mullvad.net, any *.dns.mullvad.net (base., adblock., ...) or
#      the older doh.mullvad.net is replaced by Settings.LIBREWOLF_DOH_PROVIDER_URI
#      (https://dns10.quad9.net/dns-query, the Fenix default and common.cfg's
#      network.trr.uri). The mode is not touched. Hooking the lazy engine
#      initialiser rather than an Application callback means no caller can
#      construct the engine before the migration has run. The done flag is
#      written to the same SharedPreferences as the provider, so a later Mullvad
#      URI the user enters by hand as a custom provider is respected.
#   2. When the mode was Increased or Max (DoH actually in use), a notice flag is
#      set and HomeActivity.onResume shows a one-time AlertDialog naming the new
#      provider -- the same in-app dialog mechanism update-check.patch uses. The
#      flag is cleared when the dialog is dismissed. Off/Default: silent, logged.
#   3. Mullvad leaves the built-in picker catalog, matching settings/common.cfg's
#      doh-rollout.provider-list (Redoubt-settings 0cae8fb dropped the Android
#      override that still listed it). DefaultDohSettingsProviderTest follows.
#
#
# Ordering
# ---------
# After privacy-defaults.patch: the DohSettingsProvider.kt and
# DefaultDohSettingsProviderTest.kt hunks edit text that patch creates
# (declared in scripts/check-patch-order.py). Core.kt (fission-isolation,
# ubo-preinstall) and HomeActivity.kt (no-nimbus, no-adjust, no-suggest,
# update-check, ubo-preinstall, sync-opt-in) hunks have upstream-only context,
# far from every other patch's hunks; recorded order-free.
#
#
# Verification
# -------------
#   ./mach gradle fenix:testDebugUnitTest --tests '*DohProviderMigrationTest' \
#       --tests '*DefaultDohSettingsProviderTest'
#   Not compiled when written (no Gecko AAR on the authoring host); stage B of
#   the 153.4.0esr rebase builds it.
